{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/343572-angelic-glitches","id":343572,"title":"Angelic Glitches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-17T19:53:40-08:00","id":343572,"title":"Angelic Glitches","content":"I've been binge-watching Marble Hornets today, and at some point, I began to imagine the series interpreted through the lens of <i>Demon</i>. The protagonists could be seen as Stigmatics, while the Operator makes for an interesting (and creepy) angel.<br /> <br /> Though, something's kind of off with it, huh?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this got me thinking about angels who have been damaged or corrupted. Not necessarily exiles, and not necessarily on the edge of Falling. Just angels whose existence and connection to the God-Machine is, or has become, imperfect.<br /> <br /> I imagine this would most often happen from supporting Infrastructure accruing damage. A demon breaks a vital gear or disrupts a cult's summoning ritual. The angel still comes through, but it's wrong in some ways.<br /> <br /> Its Numina might have strange side-effects. Crossing into or out of Twilight might jam local radio frequencies. Or a Numen that rewrites a target's memories might cause terrible madness instead. Maybe it shifts in and out of Twilight seemingly at random. Maybe damaging its Infrastructure after its already manifested changes its Ban, or even gives it an additional one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, these are just some thoughts I'm having. It'd give the Unchained a way to knock a powerful angel down a peg, if they know what they're doing, or turn a powerful angel into a dangerously unpredictable angel, if they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:25:24-08:00","id":343985,"title":"","content":"I've only just googled Marble Hornets so i'm going of what your saying but actually this is something that should be the default assumption.<br /> <br /> I get the reason it isn't is that most Wod games the players are the monsters and having &quot;unreliable&quot; powers seems shity on paper. plus it takes a lot of writing space to describe the side effects. but long term effect; going made form mind control, disrupting electronic frequencies, causing statues to weep and animals to behave strangely are all great horror troupes that add atmosphere and tone.<br /> <br /> This all being said Demon is partially a spy game and Angels are supposed to be one of the more subtle monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:14:35-08:00","id":344336,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to view part of the function of angelic Cover as a containment mechanism for the usual omens and auras that accompany any particular supernatural being's manifestation. Magic is leaky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T08:39:51-08:00","id":344818,"title":"","content":"Magic is leaky. That's a good phrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T11:06:16-08:00","id":344972,"title":"","content":"Angels, being Ephermeral beings, don't get wound penalties- however, I think the idea of a glitch as the equivalent would be very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}